---
import ProposalGuide from "../../components/ProposalGuide.astro";
import Deadline from "../../components/Deadline.astro";
import { cfpPages, cfpEmail } from "../../data/cfp";
---

<ProposalGuide
  lang="en"
  title="Proposal Guide"
  heroTitle="Proposal Guide"
  heroSubtitle="How to write a great submission"
  imageAlt="Retro computer showing the PyCon CZ logo next to the Pilsen cathedral tower"
  switchLink={{ label: "Přepnout na českou verzi", href: cfpPages.guideCs, lang: "cs" }}
  headings={{
    general: "General advice for talks and workshops",
    talks: "Talks",
    workshops: "Workshops",
    feedback: "Seek feedback and enjoy the process",
    cta: "Ready to submit?",
  }}
  ctaButton="Submit a proposal"
>
  <Fragment slot="intro">
    <p>
      Welcome to <strong>PyCon&nbsp;CZ&nbsp;27</strong>, the biggest and friendliest Python conference in the Czech
      Republic! We are excited to invite you to submit your proposal for a&nbsp;talk or workshop.
    </p>
    <p>
      Whether you are an experienced speaker or new to the conference scene, this guide will help you create
      a&nbsp;compelling submission. Talks can be in English or Czech: we prefer English, which every attendee
      understands, and Czech works best for talks aimed at beginners. For the tracks, formats, and speaker support, see
      the
      <a href={cfpPages.cfp}>Call for Proposals</a>.
    </p>
  </Fragment>

  <ol class="pc-numbered" slot="general">
    <li>
      <strong>Embrace your unique perspective:</strong> Your experiences and viewpoints matter, no matter where you come from.
      Share your knowledge and insights, even if they seem ordinary. Your contributions can be valuable to someone in the
      audience.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Start with an engaging title:</strong> Create a&nbsp;clear and captivating title that reflects the essence of
      your presentation. Avoid overly technical terms and strive to grab attention.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Focus on your goal:</strong> Clearly define the objective of your talk or workshop. What do you want participants
      to gain, learn, or take away? Be specific and concise to help potential attendees understand the value you will provide.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Craft an intriguing description:</strong> Provide a&nbsp;brief and compelling overview of your talk or workshop.
      Outline the topics you will cover and highlight key takeaways that participants will gain. Include practical examples
      or applications to help them relate to your content.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Showcase your past work:</strong> Consider adding links to any publicly recorded talks, published blog posts,
      or relevant materials that demonstrate your expertise and speaking ability.
    </li>
  </ol>

  <ol class="pc-numbered" slot="talks">
    <li>
      <strong>Share your expertise and passion:</strong> Infuse your talk with your enthusiasm and subject matter expertise.
      Convey your excitement about the opportunity to share your knowledge and empower others. Your unique experiences give
      you valuable insights.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Structure and flow:</strong> Ensure that your talk proposal has a&nbsp;logical structure and a&nbsp;smooth flow.
      Divide it into clear sections: introduction, main points, details, and conclusion. This will help reviewers follow your
      intended progression.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Learn from experts:</strong> Explore useful resources like <a href="https://speaking.io/">speaking.io</a> and
      the book <a href="https://www.goodreads.com/book/show/6918930-confessions-of-a-public-speaker"
        >Confessions of a&nbsp;Public Speaker</a
      > for further guidance on improving your speaking skills.
    </li>
  </ol>

  <ol class="pc-numbered" slot="workshops">
    <li>
      <strong>Incorporate interactivity:</strong> Describe how you plan to engage participants in your workshop. Explain interactive
      exercises, live coding, group discussions, or hands-on activities that will make the workshop dynamic and engaging.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Provide a&nbsp;detailed plan:</strong> Create a&nbsp;comprehensive plan for your workshop, including thematic
      areas and skills that participants will acquire.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Specify any requirements:</strong> What should the attendees know beforehand? Do they need to bring hardware
      (a&nbsp;laptop) or install software in advance?
    </li>
  </ol>

  <Fragment slot="feedback">
    <p>
      Don’t hesitate to seek feedback from colleagues, collaborators, or mentors. Ask them to evaluate your submission
      and provide constructive criticism. Work on refining your proposal and present your best ideas.
    </p>
    <p>
      Be authentic, true to yourself, and embrace the opportunity to contribute to PyCon&nbsp;CZ&nbsp;27! If you have
      any questions, please reach out to us at <a href={`mailto:${cfpEmail}`}>{cfpEmail}</a>.
    </p>
  </Fragment>

  <Fragment slot="cta">
    <p>
      Now that you know how, go ahead and submit your proposal. We look forward to reviewing your submissions and
      welcoming you as a&nbsp;speaker or workshop facilitator!
    </p>
    <p><strong>Deadline: <Deadline lang="en" /></strong></p>
  </Fragment>
</ProposalGuide>
